# EXPECTATION FOR LANE RUN 20 — derived and committed ALONE, BEFORE the run (D0A-R21-07).
#
# Target commit: 29a0590. The instrument was frozen one commit earlier (29a0590) so this
# prediction is about the code that will actually run, not a different version of it.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE DERIVATION — checkable independently of whether the number matches
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 19 measured root 216 / 5 / 221 at c10810f. Six test identities have been added since
# and NONE removed, giving 227 reported. Enumerated from the diff, not from memory — and the
# first enumeration was WRONG: the grep used `fn [a-z_]+`, which excludes digits, so every
# test with `b1` in its name was invisible, including the one this run exists for. Corrected
# to `[a-z0-9_]+`. A derivation produced by a grep is only as sound as the grep.
#
#   test                                                    | file                | root gate
#   --------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|----------
#   an_already_dead_childs_exit_code_survives_shutdown       | shutdown.rs         | NONE
#   a_child_that_died_of_a_signal_is_not_reported_as_clean   | shutdown.rs         | NONE
#   reap_status_retries_a_waitpid_interrupted_by_a_signal    | test_child_guard.rs | NONE
#   live_group_members_..._skips_a_real_zombie               | b1_integration.rs   | NONE
#   strip_ansi_recovers_the_field_text_tracing_actually_emits| b1_integration.rs   | NONE
#   b1_daemon_bounds_an_ai_..._and_stays_alive               | b1_integration.rs   | feature+
#                                                           |                     | root+bwrap
#
# Gates verified by grep of the 25 lines following each `fn`, per the procedure's "never from
# memory" clause. Five are ungated and run in both lanes. The sixth checks the FEATURE FIRST,
# so it skips in BOTH lanes here: the lane builds without `--features insecure-test-seams`.
#
#   EXECUTED  216 + 5 = 221
#   SKIPPED     5 + 1 =   6      (the five from run 19, plus the assembly test's feature skip)
#   reported  221 + 6 = 227      (agrees with the measured unprivileged 201/26/227)
#
# Cross-check: unprivileged went 196/25/221 -> 201/26/227, i.e. +5 executed and +1 skipped,
# which is the same partition of the same six tests. If root reports anything other than
# 221/6/227, ONE of these two statements is false and the mismatch is the result.
#
# =========================================================================================
# RUN 20 HAS TWO PARTS, AND THE SECOND IS THE POINT
# =========================================================================================
#
# PART A — the standard 17-target lane, built WITHOUT the feature. This is the count evidence
# and it stays comparable to run 19. It does NOT execute the assembly test.
#
# PART B — a SEPARATE root execution of the assembly test WITH `--features
# insecure-test-seams`, which is how the previous five assembly runs were done. Part B does
# not contribute to the counts above and must not be folded into them.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE CONTROL'S POSSIBLE OUTCOMES, NAMED BEFORE THE RUN
# =========================================================================================
#
# The control asserts the scanner saw the real AI ALIVE in the daemon's process group. Three
# outcomes, and they are not equally informative:
#
# 1. CONTROL PASSES, survivors empty, nine assertions pass.
#    The scanner is proven capable in the assembly, not merely in a fixture. This is the only
#    outcome in which the empty sample is evidence about the daemon.
#
# 2. CONTROL FAILS, census EMPTY.
#    The daemon's group never contained any member the scan could see. **This is a PRODUCT /
#    ARCHITECTURE finding** and it contradicts the reasoning the closure rests on — that
#    neither launcher.rs nor execute.rs calls setsid/setpgid, so forked children inherit the
#    pgid. It would mean the empty sample has never meant what the register says.
#
# 3. CONTROL FAILS, census NON-EMPTY but containing no member named as the AI.
#    The scan reaches the group; the AI was not identified in it. **This is a defect in the
#    CONTROL** — a comm mismatch (the staged name is truncated to 15 bytes by the kernel) or a
#    window the 25 ms poll missed — and it is evidence about my instrument, not about the
#    daemon. Do NOT report it as a product finding, and do not report it as a harness artifact
#    either until the census SHOWS it (Iron Law 15 clause 5: the harness is guilty only when
#    shown to be).
#
# Outcomes 2 and 3 both present as "POSITIVE CONTROL FAILED". The census is what separates
# them, which is why the probe was changed to retain one before this file was written.
#
# A fourth outcome is possible and is not a control failure: the control passes and
# `survivors_before_guard` is NON-EMPTY. That is the daemon failing to clean up, caught by
# the assertion that already exists.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHAT EACH OUTCOME DOES TO D0A-R28-02'S CLOSURE
# =========================================================================================
#
# ON A PASS the register's wording STRENGTHENS, from
#
#     "No live group members remained before harness intervention; daemon reaping was not
#      observed."
#
# to
#
#     "The scanner was proven capable of seeing the daemon's own fork/exec'd child in its
#      inherited process group, and no live group members remained before harness
#      intervention; daemon reaping was not observed."
#
# The reaping clause does NOT change — this run observes cleanup, not reaping, and R29-05's
# `Unreaped` branch stays UNCONSTRUCTED.
#
# ON A FAILURE OF KIND 2 the CLOSURE WITHDRAWS — not the test. The test would have done
# exactly its job. D0A-R28-02 returns to OPEN with the reason recorded, and the fixture
# demonstration is marked as not transferring to the assembly.
#
# ON A FAILURE OF KIND 3 nothing about the closure changes and the control is fixed; the
# closure stays where it is, still resting on an argument, and says so.
#
# I do not know which of these will happen. Stating that plainly is the point of writing them
# down first: after the run, whichever occurs will feel like the one that was expected.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=221
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=6
EXPECTED_REPORTED=227
